# The emotional coda to a CONVERSATION.
#
# cli/outcome/emotion/success.cli covers the narration half. This is the other half, and it is a
# separate script because the two paths are separate code: narration resolves the emotion from the
# reports it gathered before the dice, a conversation from the outcome set the tree hands out at its
# resolution. Wiring one and not the other is exactly the kind of gap that leaves five outcome types
# unreachable by any disposition - alms, an introduction granted, an enmity cleared, a trade or a
# job opened, and a conversation that came to nothing all exist only in a tree.
#
# Copied from cli/system/dialogue_success.cli, which is a known-good walk of the meet_stranger tree,
# with --grant-mm gregariousness added (the starting kit is random, so holding a disposition that
# answers a relation moving is otherwise a coin flip) and the assertions appended.
#
# meet_stranger is deliberately the tree used, and not only because it is the cheapest to reach: it
# is the ONLY tree whose whole outcome set is one AffinityTransitionOutcome, which sets a level
# rather than stepping one and therefore carries no direction. Under the type-only rule that means
# only a direction-agnostic disposition may answer it, and until one did, the most-played tree in
# the game - the introduction, which gates every other conversation - could stir nothing at all.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer" --grant-mm gregariousness

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# --- before: no mind state in the spleen, which secretion never produces one ---
expect-no-state humors Laetitia

# Reach the conversation through the verb that opens it.
strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The tree is live. `advance` drains whichever preview box is up — the NPC's greeting, then each
# reply option, which are generated as their own stack.
wait mode Dialogue 60
advance 20 180
expect Good day
regions

# Walk a branch to its resolution. Two replies is the shortest route through this tree.
click option 0
advance 20 180
regions
click option 0
advance 20 180

# The resolution roll is settled; confirming it applies the branch's outcome.
click continue
advance 20 180

# The branch's SUCCESS replica, not its failure one — this is what tells the two apart, and so what
# proves the resolution roll was honoured rather than the tree merely reaching an end.
expect Courteous, and you know when to stop

# The coda is a preview part of its own, so it lands on its own press. `advance` drains it.
advance 20 180

# The outcome really ran, and the block reached the screen. Under --playground the persona rewrite
# returns the neutral line unchanged, so the humor's own FeelsLike sentence is on screen verbatim -
# which is what proves the coda was NARRATED, not merely chipped.
expect-outcome emotion
expect It makes me feel

# --- after: the spleen really moved ---
inspect humors
expect-state humors Laetitia
state
quit
